    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` to the spec, and the 9 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage check, so I can't confirm the 90% gate. The tests do exercise every branch I wrote.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- item validation\n- shipping at the 100.00 boundary\n- percent and fixed discounts, including the fixed cap at the subtotal\n- every `CouponError` case, including the expiry and minimum-subtotal edges\n- the `ValueError` cases for coupon values\n- half-up rounding\n\nThe spec doesn't say which check wins when a coupon fails more than one, so I check in this order: item validity, then expiry, then used code, then minimum subtotal, then kind, then value range. A bad percent value on an otherwise valid coupon raises `ValueError`, and an unknown kind raises `CouponError`. A boolean quantity is rejected as invalid.",
